From 72594e7bfcd0e497a045bfbf3951142c4091c0f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.local>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 19:27:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ADR-0006: presence-corroborated decline can end a session
 from ACTIVE

Fixes a real incident: a session peaked at 84.4% RH, declined steadily
for over an hour, but plateaued at 54-59% -- still above the frozen
session_start_threshold (~52-53%, baseline + humidity_start_delta=3.0).
Because it never dropped back below that threshold, _from_active never
transitioned to COOLDOWN, so none of ADR-0005's decline/presence checks
(which live entirely in _from_cooldown) ever ran. The session's
binary_sensor stayed 'on' for 8+ hours, for the rest of the logged day.

Presence data showed the room was confirmed empty (continuously False)
for 67 minutes starting 5 minutes after the peak -- strong, independent
evidence the shower had ended, that the old logic had no way to use
because it was still waiting to cross an absolute floor.

Fix: track the decline-from-peak and presence-clear timers continuously
from ACTIVE onward (previously COOLDOWN-only), via a new shared
_update_decline_and_presence_tracking() helper. If a decline from peak
is corroborated by presence continuously clear for
presence_clear_confirm_seconds, the session now ends directly from
ACTIVE -- skipping COOLDOWN entirely -- regardless of the absolute
humidity level.

Deliberately scoped to the presence-corroborated path only. The
no-presence decline_confirmed path (ADR-0005) stays COOLDOWN-only,
per ADR-0005's own "Alternatives Considered": without presence
corroboration, a temporary dip mid-shower must not be able to end a
session that's still genuinely running. Sessions without a configured
presence sensor are not fixed by this ADR -- tracked in BACKLOG.md,
alongside a proposed max_active_seconds hard backstop as a follow-up.

- session.py: new _update_decline_and_presence_tracking() and
  _end_session() helpers shared by _from_active/_from_cooldown.
  _from_active gains a presence param and the early-exit check.
  update()'s ACTIVE dispatch now passes presence through. No config
  or wiring changes needed -- presence was already threaded into every
  detector.update() call site from ADR-0005.
- const.py / __init__.py / manifest.json: version bump only (1.7.0).
- Tests: 5 new tests (4 in test_session.py incl. a regression test
  replaying the incident's humidity/presence shape, 1 end-to-end wiring
  test in test_init.py). Full suite: 110 passed (105 previously passing
  + 5 new).
- README.md / BACKLOG.md updated.

See adr/ADR-0006-decline-confirmed-end-during-active.md for full
rationale, including why the no-presence path is deliberately not
extended the same way.
